# Module/page:
Tasks tab project dropdown and individual task detail view

# Current problem:
The Tasks tab project dropdown only shows the project name. This is confusing because users cannot easily tell which company/customer the project belongs to.

Inside an individual task, there is not enough project context. Users cannot clearly see the overall project name, company/customer, or related project details.

Also, a task can only be assigned to one person. Some tasks need multiple assigned users.

# Desired behavior:
In the Tasks tab project dropdown:
- Display company/customer name followed by project name
- Format: Company Name - Project Name

Inside each task detail view:
- Show the project/company context clearly at the top or top-side section
- At minimum show:
  - Company/customer name
  - Project name
  - Project code/number if available
- All assigned users should see the same project details

Task assignment:
- Allow multiple users to be assigned to the same task
- All assigned users should see the task in their Tasks tab
- Existing single-assignee tasks should continue working

# UI requirements:
Tasks tab:
- Keep the same overall Tasks tab layout
- Keep existing project dropdown behavior
- Only change the dropdown label format to:
  Company Name - Project Name

Task detail view:
- Keep existing task detail layout/navigation
- Add project details near the top of the task detail view
- Do not redesign the whole task modal/page

Assignees:
- Replace or extend the existing assignee selector to support multiple users
- Display multiple assigned users clearly
- Do not remove existing assigned user behavior

# Database involved:
- projects table
- tasks table
- users table

Likely needs review of current assignment structure:
- If tasks currently only support one assignee_id, propose safest way to support multiple assignees.
- Do not change schema until plan is reviewed and approved.

# What must NOT change:
- Do NOT change overall Tasks tab navigation
- Do NOT change project creation flow
- Do NOT redesign task cards or task detail layout
- Do NOT break existing task filtering
- Do NOT remove existing single-assignee compatibility
- Do NOT affect existing tasks unless migration/backfill is explicitly approved

# Workflow step-by-step:
1. User opens Tasks tab
2. User opens project filter dropdown
3. Project options show as:
   Company Name - Project Name
4. User filters/selects tasks as usual
5. User opens an individual task
6. Task detail clearly shows project/company context near the top
7. If multiple users are assigned to the task:
   - each assigned user sees the task in their own Tasks tab
   - task details remain the same for all assigned users
8. Admin/user with permission can assign or remove multiple users from the task